# Tech Stack

- Backend: Python. Orchestrator/worker loop follows the orchestrator-worker (supervisor) pattern.
- Orchestration framework: LangGraph (create_supervisor) unless a ticket's design.md says otherwise.
- Model tiering: strong hosted model (Claude/GPT-class) for the orchestrator and any worker doing
  multi-step reasoning. Local Ollama models are allowed only for narrow, well-defined worker tasks
  with low reasoning depth.
- Event transport: WebSockets. Orchestrator/worker lifecycle events (spawned, thinking, tool_call,
  subagent_spawned, completed, error) are emitted as structured events, not free text.
- Event/API server: FastAPI on uvicorn, with `websockets` as the WebSocket implementation. The
  orchestrator runs as a persistent process serving `WS /events` plus a small HTTP surface for
  submitting goals; `orchestrator.run` stays as a one-shot CLI for runs that need no dashboard.
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + React Flow for the node-based board. No game engine (no Phaser).
  Gamified visual elements (progress bars, status badges) are CSS/component-level only.
- Prompts: stored as versioned files under prompts/<worker-name>/vN.md. Never edit a prompt file
  without running its golden-set eval first.
- Do not add a new framework/library without updating this file in the same PR.
